Z||000012||Oreif||10-28-2001||10:23 AM||||With my first Fiero I drove under 2 trucks.<BR>The car was not lowered. The first truck was at a Mack truck repair center. (Friends Dad worked there) The only trailer it would fit under was a Mack Super Cushion trailer. The ONLY reason it fit under it was because it had shocks on the trailer supports and no center brace. Most trailers have a center brace that hangs down 4". The trailer I drove unde was parked and EMPTY. I had to close the sunroof to clear it. The second truck I drove under was a truck that jack-knifed across a road. The cab was tilted sideways which raise the trailer about a foot. I think many cars could have fit under it. The police officer on the other side of the truck didn't find it as humorus as I did.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> (Actually I was running late and trying to get to work in my young and foolish days) <P>With my present Fiero lowered 1.5" I still don't think it will fit under a standard semi trailer. The brace down the middle hangs down too much. Also I wouldn't recommend driving to a truckstop and trying it. I don't know the real numbers but I bet a fully loaded trailer is lower than an empty one.<P>------------------<BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">          <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><B><I>Happiness isn't around the corner...<BR>Happiness IS the corner.</I></B></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000013||85 gt fiero||10-28-2001||10:28 AM||||If you go fast enough the bottom of the semi trailer will take care off the convertibale problem for you, it might also knock some sense into your head.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> Randy<P>------------------<BR>RALLY CAR, FULL ROLL CAGE, SKID PLATES AND SOON TO BE BRIGHT YELLOW||||reg||1
Z||000014||Haagster||10-28-2001||10:51 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by grinthock:<BR><B>I fit my  85 GT under one of those REALLY high intermodal box trucks once, it was parked, It LOOKED like it would fit, I got out, looked/measured (basically) then inched my way under, it fit with like 3 millimeters of space to spare.<P>A Safe Stunt.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Measured and Parked.  Not the same as doing the suicide run at highway speed.<P>BTW, is 3mm enough to allow the air ride system on most trailers to flex without caving in the roof of your car?  I think not...<P>||||reg||13
